From 6b703970ef488a90f479fba164801664a8a7addd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:03:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Reaper settings export / import; diag: /jffs health finding

The Reaper lists left nvram (v2.6.3 / v2.6.7 / v2.6.9) so the stock nvram
backup no longer carries them. reaper_cfg.cgi (Storage page, "Reaper
settings backup") exports one JSON file: Gatekeeper flags + device list,
Policy Routing flag + rules, the Firewall engine's flags + eight lists, and
Warden's nvram keys (allowlisted). Import replays each value through the
path an interactive edit takes - every value passes the same charset /
length gates as the per-page saves; the firewall and routing lists are
STAGED as drafts so commit-confirm still gates anything that could lock the
operator out; Gatekeeper's list and Warden's keys (no confirm step) are
written and their services restarted. Nothing touches /jffs/configs.

Diag v1.3.4: /jffs total/used/free, read-only state, a write test, and the
space Reaper's stores take; WARN when unmounted, read-only, under 2 MB free
/ over 90 %, or the write test fails - the lists live only there now.
